 "case:locations.compound.art.props.5.label": "Gate",
 "case:locations.compound.description": "A fenced lot behind Barnstaple police station, where vehicles wait for the coroner. Moss is at the end of the row under a grey cover, an evidence label on the windscreen. A civilian examiner, Mr Hosking, walks you over and lifts the cover: Callum’s solicitor has arranged it. You may look, and photograph, but not remove anything.",
 "case:locations.compound.hotspots.hs_pc_alarm.label": "Moss — CO alarm",
 "case:locations.compound.hotspots.hs_pc_alarm.text": "A carbon monoxide alarm with a little screen, screwed to the wall by the sliding door at pillow height.",
 "case:locations.compound.hotspots.hs_pc_glovebox.label": "Moss — glovebox",
 "case:locations.compound.hotspots.hs_pc_glovebox.text": "Insurance papers, a parking receipt from Saunton, a tyre gauge, and Moss’s latest MOT certificate.",
 "case:locations.compound.hotspots.hs_pc_label.label": "The evidence label",
 "case:locations.compound.hotspots.hs_pc_label.text": "‘Exhibit — VW Transporter. Examined 20/11. Released: NOT YET — CORONER.’ Mr Hosking says the coroner’s officer wants Moss kept until the inquest, and Trading Standards want photographs of every fitting.",
 "case:locations.compound.hotspots.hs_pc_pocket.label": "Moss — door pocket",
 "case:locations.compound.hotspots.hs_pc_pocket.text": "In the pocket of the sliding door: a head torch, a tide table, a bag of jelly babies and the alarm’s folded leaflet.",
 "case:locations.compound.hotspots.hs_pc_seat.label": "Moss — passenger seat",
 "case:locations.compound.hotspots.hs_pc_seat.text": "Mr Hosking slides the door open for you. The passenger seat base lifts off on four screws. Underneath sits the diesel heater, a grey box the size of a shoebox, with its exhaust pipe dropping through the floor.",
 "case:locations.compound.name": "Police Compound",
 "case:locations.compound.summary": "Where Moss is kept, behind Barnstaple police station.",
